// This Source Code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0
// O→D Vortex Live — the causal (non-repainting) version of the O→D vortex idea.

//@version=6
indicator("O→D Vortex Live — دوامة O→D الحيّة", shorttitle = "VORTEX LIVE", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_polylines_count = 20)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT THIS IS
//
// @dimitri41201857 posted a 30-second video of a 3D indicator on US500 2h: price "revolves"
// around a straight vector drawn from a swing point O to a swing point D, inside two
// half-ellipse walls; touching a wall is a "potential trade" back toward the vector.
// engine/vortex.js in this repository reproduces every readout on his screenshots exactly.
//
// THE VIDEO'S VERSION CANNOT BE TRADED. In it, D, the walls and the angle θ are all measured
// on the FINISHED swing: the walls are sized from the window's own largest deviations, so every
// window shows wall contacts at exactly ±1 by construction, whatever the market did, and D is a
// low nobody could know at the time. Live, with D still in the future, none of it exists.
// Earlier tests here (reports/vortex-replay.txt, reports/vortex-forecast.txt) found no live
// edge in it on US500 2h / 4h or SPX daily.
//
// This script is the causal version — "Vortex Live" v1, a spec fixed on 2026-10-03 before any
// per-timeframe result was seen, and not tuned afterwards. Every piece is built from what is
// known at the close of the bar it is drawn on:
//
//   1. pivots      ATR(14) computed as Pine ta.atr; a zigzag whose reversal threshold is
//                  4 × ATR / close of the CURRENT bar. A pivot exists from the bar that
//                  confirms it, never earlier, and its marker is drawn back at its own bar.
//   2. windows     each completed swing gives n (bars), size |ln(P1/P0)| and, for n ≥ 4, the
//                  wall ratios Wup/|ΔP| and Wdn/|ΔP| measured the video's way on that swing.
//   3. projection  when a pivot O is confirmed: from the last K = 5 swings,
//                  N = max(8, median n), D = O × exp(∓ median size) against the swing that
//                  ended at O, walls = |D − O| × median ratios. It stays live until the next
//                  pivot is confirmed.
//   4. entry       on a bar close, flat, once per projection, outside the first and last 3 %
//                  of N: 0.85 ≤ |e| < 1.25 → fade the wall. شراء (buy) under the vector,
//                  بيع (sell) above it. e = (OHLC4 − vector) / (wall × ellipse).
//   5. exit        on a later close, against the ENTRY projection: ⏱ time once past N − skip,
//                  else ✕ stop at |e| ≥ 1.25 on the entry side, else ✓ target at the vector.
//   6. return      side × (exit − entry) / entry − round-trip cost. A win is a return > 0.
//   7.             one position at a time; an open trade keeps its own projection.
//
// It mirrors engine/vortex-live.js bar for bar: same pivots, projections, entries and exits on
// the same bars (the JS is the source of truth and is tested rule by rule there). The ATR is
// computed by hand in the reference's order of operations rather than with ta.atr(): the two
// agree to 1e-12, but the zigzag threshold is a comparison, and only identical arithmetic
// guarantees identical pivots. To reproduce the JS numbers exactly, run the JS from the same
// first bar the chart loads — the ATR seed and the zigzag start both depend on it.
//
// NON-REPAINT. Signals, labels and alerts appear only on closed bars, and a signal, exit or
// pivot marker is never moved once drawn (TradingView only drops the oldest beyond 500). A
// realtime bar counts as closed on its last update; on history a bar counts as closed only once
// its time_close has passed, so a last bar loaded while the market is shut and still forming
// (a weekly bar mid-week, a monthly bar mid-month, a 4H bar across a session break) is not
// treated as closed. The live projection is redrawn on the last bar by design; it and the table
// show the state as of the last closed bar.
//
// STANDARD CANDLES ONLY. On Heikin Ashi, Renko, Kagi, Line Break, Point & Figure or Range
// charts Pine feeds the script synthetic prices, so every pivot, wall and signal would differ
// from the reference; the script stops with an error there. Bars, candles, hollow candles, line,
// area and baseline all use the real OHLC and are fine.
//
// THE TABLE. One row per timeframe: 4H, daily, weekly, monthly — each runs the whole engine on
// its own bars through request.security (lookahead off, last CLOSED bar only). The row for the
// chart's own timeframe (highlighted) uses the chart's own run, so it agrees with the labels on
// the chart. Other timeframes only see the history TradingView loads for them, which starts
// around the chart's first bar — so open the indicator on the weekly or monthly chart itself to
// get those rows over their full history. The "±" next to the mean return is a rough 95 %
// interval (normal approximation); green/red only when the whole interval is above/below 0.
//
// Win rate alone does not say whether this makes money: a high win rate with small wins and
// big losses loses. Judge a timeframe by the mean return per trade, its interval, and the
// profit factor — and by the null tests in the repository, which this script cannot run.
//
// KNOWN PROPERTIES OF THE SPEC (reported, not tuned)
//   - The wall ratios pool rising and falling swings, so the projected walls come out lopsided
//     (on US500 4h the first projections have the upper wall ≈ 4.7 × the lower one).
//   - Sample size: about one trade per 50 bars on 4h. Weekly and monthly charts produce very
//     few trades; any win rate there has a very wide interval.
//   - With a per-bar threshold, a pivot is not always the extreme between its neighbours.
//
// MEASURED RESULT — READ THIS BEFORE TRADING IT
//
//   [placeholder — to be filled with the per-timeframe measurement]
//   timeframe   data   trades   win rate [95 %]   median / mean hold   expectancy [95 %]   PF   vs matched chance
//   4H          …      …        …                 …                    …                   …    …
//   1D          …      …        …                 …                    …                   …    …
//   1W          …      …        …                 …                    …                   …    …
//   1M          …      …        …                 …                    …                   …    …
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ── constants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Stands in for ±∞ where a wall has zero width (the JS uses Infinity). Any value above the
// stop level behaves the same: never an entry, and as an exit it reads by the side of the vector.
float VL_E_BIG            = 1000000000000.0
int   VL_MIN_WALL_N       = 4     // a swing shorter than this gives n and size, but no wall ratios
int   VL_MIN_WALL_WINDOWS = 3     // a projection needs this many of its K swings with wall ratios
int   VL_MIN_N            = 8     // the projected N is at least this (spec: minN = 8)
int   VL_FUTURE           = 499   // drawings may reach at most 500 bars past the last bar
int   VL_NCOL             = 8     // table columns
int   VL_NROW             = 7     // table rows

color VL_BUY   = #26a69a
color VL_SELL  = #ef5350
color VL_VEC   = #b2b5be
color VL_TBG   = color.new(#131722, 8)
color VL_THL   = color.new(#2a3550, 0)
color VL_THEAD = color.new(#1e222d, 0)
color VL_WARN  = #ffa726
color VL_MUTED = #787b86

// ── inputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
string VL_G_ENGINE = "المحرك — Engine (spec v1; keep the defaults to compare with the measurement)"
string VL_G_VIEW   = "العرض — Display"

int   atrLenIn  = input.int(14, "طول ATR", minval = 1, maxval = 500, group = VL_G_ENGINE, tooltip = "ATR length. Computed as Pine ta.atr with the reference's exact arithmetic: first true range = high − low, seeded by the simple mean of the first N true ranges, then Wilder's RMA. Spec: 14.")
float atrMultIn = input.float(4.0, "مضاعف ATR للانعكاس", minval = 0.1, maxval = 50.0, step = 0.5, group = VL_G_ENGINE, tooltip = "Zigzag reversal threshold = this multiple × ATR / close, using the CURRENT bar's ATR and close. Spec: 4.")
int   kIn       = input.int(5, "عدد الموجات السابقة K", minval = 3, maxval = 50, group = VL_G_ENGINE, tooltip = "How many completed swings feed the medians that project N, D and the walls. Spec: 5.")
float levelIn   = input.float(0.85, "مستوى ملامسة الجدار", minval = 0.05, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.05, group = VL_G_ENGINE, tooltip = "Contact level. Enter when contact ≤ |e| < stop; e = ±1 on the walls and 0 on the vector. Spec: 0.85.")
float stopIn    = input.float(1.25, "مستوى الوقف", minval = 0.1, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.05, group = VL_G_ENGINE, tooltip = "Stop when |e| reaches this on the entry side. It is also the upper edge of the entry band. Spec: 1.25.")
float skipIn    = input.float(3.0, "تجاهل قرب O و D (%)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 49.0, step = 0.5, group = VL_G_ENGINE, tooltip = "Ignore near O and D: no entries in the first and last X % of the projected N, and a trade still open after N − skip exits on time. Spec: 3 %.")
float costIn    = input.float(0.02, "التكلفة ذهاباً وإياباً (%)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.01, group = VL_G_ENGINE, tooltip = "Round-trip cost subtracted from every trade's return, in percent: 0.02 for indices, gold and FX; 0.10 for crypto.")

bool   showTableIn = input.bool(true, "جدول الدقة لكل فريم", group = VL_G_VIEW, tooltip = "Per-timeframe table: trades, win rate, typical and mean duration, mean return per trade with a rough 95 % interval, profit factor, and how much history each row is based on.")
bool   showProjIn  = input.bool(true, "الإسقاط الحي (المتجه والجداران)", group = VL_G_VIEW, tooltip = "Draw the live projection: the vector O → projected D (dashed) and the two half-ellipse walls. While a trade is open under an older projection, that one is drawn too, faded.")
bool   showBandIn  = input.bool(true, "نطاق الملامسة", group = VL_G_VIEW, tooltip = "Dotted lines at the contact level (0.85 of each wall): an entry needs the bar's OHLC4 beyond them and inside the wall × stop level.")
bool   showPivIn   = input.bool(true, "القمم والقيعان المؤكدة", group = VL_G_VIEW, tooltip = "Mark each pivot at its own bar, drawn on the bar that confirmed it.")
string tablePosIn  = input.string("أعلى اليمين", "موضع الجدول", options = ["أعلى اليمين", "أعلى اليسار", "أسفل اليمين", "أسفل اليسار"], group = VL_G_VIEW, tooltip = "Table position: top right, top left, bottom right, bottom left.")

if levelIn >= stopIn
    runtime.error("مستوى الملامسة يجب أن يكون أقل من مستوى الوقف — the contact level must be below the stop level.")
if not chart.is_standard
    runtime.error("استخدم الشموع العادية — the engine needs standard candles (not Heikin Ashi, Renko, Kagi, Line Break, Point & Figure or Range).")

float vlSkipFrac = skipIn / 100.0   // 3 → 0.03, the same double as the reference's literal
float vlCostFrac = costIn / 100.0   // 0.02 → 0.0002, likewise

// ── engine helpers (stateless) ───────────────────────────────────────────────

// Median exactly as the reference: copy, sort ascending; odd count → the middle value,
// even count → the mean of the two middle values. na for an empty array.
vlMedian(array<float> xs) =>
    float result = na
    int c = array.size(xs)
    if c > 0
        array<float> s = array.copy(xs)
        array.sort(s, order.ascending)
        int m = int(math.floor(c / 2.0))
        result := c % 2 == 1 ? array.get(s, m) : (array.get(s, m - 1) + array.get(s, m)) / 2.0
    result

// Position e of `price` against a projection (PO, PD, N, Wup, Wdn), i bars after O:
// e = (price − vector) / (W_side × ellipse). A zero-width wall reads ±VL_E_BIG by the side of
// the vector, and 0 exactly on it.
vlPositionE(float PO, float PD, int N, float wUp, float wDn, int i, float price) =>
    float vec = PO + ((PD - PO) * i) / N
    float u = 2.0 * i / N - 1.0
    float shp = math.sqrt(math.max(0.0, 1.0 - u * u))
    float dev = price - vec
    float W = dev > 0 ? wUp : wDn
    float wall = W * shp
    float e = wall > 0 ? dev / wall : dev > 0 ? VL_E_BIG : dev < 0 ? -VL_E_BIG : 0.0
    e

// A completed swing a → b: n, size = |ln(pb/pa)| and, for n ≥ 4, the wall ratios the video's
// construction gives on it (price pinned to the pivot prices at both ends — those two points
// have ellipse 0 and never count — OHLC4 inside, skip = round(skipFrac × n)), as fractions of
// |pb − pa|. `o4s` holds OHLC4 by bar, element 0 being bar `o4Base`.
vlMeasureWindow(array<float> o4s, int o4Base, int ia, float pa, int ib, float pb, float skipFrac) =>
    int   n  = ib - ia
    float sz = math.abs(math.log(pb / pa))
    float ru = na
    float rd = na
    if n >= VL_MIN_WALL_N and pb != pa
        int   skip = math.round(skipFrac * n)
        float wUp  = 0.0
        float wDn  = 0.0
        if n - skip >= skip
            for i = skip to n - skip
                float u   = 2.0 * i / n - 1.0
                float shp = math.sqrt(math.max(0.0, 1.0 - u * u))
                int   k   = ia + i - o4Base
                if shp > 0 and k >= 0 and k < array.size(o4s)
                    float p = array.get(o4s, k)
                    if not na(p)
                        float vec = pa + ((pb - pa) * i) / n
                        float dev = p - vec
                        wUp := math.max(wUp, dev / shp)
                        wDn := math.max(wDn, -dev / shp)
        float span = math.abs(pb - pa)
        ru := wUp / span
        rd := wDn / span
    [n, sz, ru, rd]

// ── the engine: one bar-by-bar state machine ─────────────────────────────────
// Called once per bar, unconditionally, by each user (the chart, and one request.security per
// timeframe); every call site keeps its own state. Order inside a bar: ATR → zigzag (pivot,
// window, projection) → exit of the open trade → entry. Returns only simple values.
vortexCore(int atrLen, float atrMult, int K, float level, float stopE, float skipFrac, int minN, float cost) =>
    int   t  = bar_index
    bool  ok = not na(open) and not na(high) and not na(low) and not na(close) and close > 0
    float o4 = ok ? (open + high + low + close) / 4 : na

    var int firstTime = time
    var int nBars = 0
    nBars += 1

    // Own OHLC4 history, so no loop ever indexes series history with a dynamic offset.
    // Element 0 is bar o4Base; bars before the last confirmed pivot are dropped (never needed).
    var array<float> o4s = array.new<float>()
    var int o4Base = bar_index
    array.push(o4s, o4)

    // 1a. ATR — Pine ta.atr(atrLen), in the reference's exact arithmetic.
    var float atrPrevClose = na
    var int   atrCount     = 0
    var float atrSum       = 0.0
    var float atrVal       = na
    float thr = na
    if ok
        float tr = na(atrPrevClose) ? high - low : math.max(math.max(high - low, math.abs(high - atrPrevClose)), math.abs(low - atrPrevClose))
        atrPrevClose := close
        if na(atrVal)
            atrSum   += tr
            atrCount += 1
            if atrCount == atrLen
                atrVal := atrSum / atrLen
        else
            float alpha = 1.0 / atrLen
            atrVal := alpha * tr + (1.0 - alpha) * atrVal
        if not na(atrVal)
            thr := (atrMult * atrVal) / close

    // 1b. Zigzag with the current bar's threshold. Starts on the first bar with an ATR.
    var bool  zzStarted = false
    var int   zzDir     = 0
    var int   hiIdx     = na
    var float hiPx      = na
    var int   loIdx     = na
    var float loPx      = na
    var int   cIdx      = na
    var float cPx       = na
    int   pvKind = 0      // +1 a high was confirmed on this bar, −1 a low, 0 none
    int   pvIdx  = na
    float pvPx   = na
    if not na(thr)
        if not zzStarted
            zzStarted := true
            hiIdx := t
            hiPx  := high
            loIdx := t
            loPx  := low
            int dropStart = t - o4Base
            if dropStart > 0
                o4s    := array.copy(array.slice(o4s, dropStart, array.size(o4s)))
                o4Base := t
        else if zzDir == 0
            if high > hiPx
                hiIdx := t
                hiPx  := high
            if low < loPx
                loIdx := t
                loPx  := low
            if loIdx < hiIdx and hiPx >= loPx * (1 + thr)
                zzDir  := 1
                cIdx   := hiIdx
                cPx    := hiPx
                pvKind := -1
                pvIdx  := loIdx
                pvPx   := loPx
            else if hiIdx < loIdx and loPx <= hiPx * (1 - thr)
                zzDir  := -1
                cIdx   := loIdx
                cPx    := loPx
                pvKind := 1
                pvIdx  := hiIdx
                pvPx   := hiPx
        else if zzDir == 1
            if high > cPx
                cIdx := t
                cPx  := high
            else if low <= cPx * (1 - thr)
                pvKind := 1
                pvIdx  := cIdx
                pvPx   := cPx
                zzDir  := -1
                cIdx   := t
                cPx    := low
        else
            if low < cPx
                cIdx := t
                cPx  := low
            else if high >= cPx * (1 + thr)
                pvKind := -1
                pvIdx  := cIdx
                pvPx   := cPx
                zzDir  := 1
                cIdx   := t
                cPx    := high

    // 2–3. The swing the new pivot completes, and the projection drawn from it.
    var int   pivCount   = 0
    var int   prevPivIdx = na
    var float prevPivPx  = na
    var array<float> wN  = array.new<float>()    // the last K swings: n
    var array<float> wSz = array.new<float>()    //                    size
    var array<float> wRu = array.new<float>()    //                    Wup / |ΔP| (na if n < 4)
    var array<float> wRd = array.new<float>()    //                    Wdn / |ΔP| (na if n < 4)
    var bool  gOn       = false                  // a projection is live for entries
    var int   gId       = -1
    var int   gConf     = na
    var int   gIO       = na
    var float gPO       = na
    var int   gN        = na
    var float gPD       = na
    var float gWup      = na
    var float gWdn      = na
    var int   gSkip     = na
    var int   projCount = 0
    if pvKind != 0
        pivCount += 1
        if pivCount >= 2
            [wn, wsz, wru, wrd] = vlMeasureWindow(o4s, o4Base, prevPivIdx, prevPivPx, pvIdx, pvPx, skipFrac)
            array.push(wN, float(wn))
            array.push(wSz, wsz)
            array.push(wRu, wru)
            array.push(wRd, wrd)
            if array.size(wN) > K
                array.shift(wN)
                array.shift(wSz)
                array.shift(wRu)
                array.shift(wRd)
        prevPivIdx := pvIdx
        prevPivPx  := pvPx
        int dropPiv = pvIdx - o4Base
        if dropPiv > 0
            o4s    := array.copy(array.slice(o4s, dropPiv, array.size(o4s)))
            o4Base := pvIdx
        // A new pivot ends the old projection's life for entries, projectable or not.
        gOn := false
        if array.size(wN) >= K
            array<float> rus = array.new<float>()
            array<float> rds = array.new<float>()
            for j = 0 to array.size(wRu) - 1
                float r = array.get(wRu, j)
                if not na(r)
                    array.push(rus, r)
                    array.push(rds, array.get(wRd, j))
            if array.size(rus) >= VL_MIN_WALL_WINDOWS
                bool  falling = pvKind == 1
                int   NN      = math.max(minN, math.round(vlMedian(wN)))
                float mSize   = vlMedian(wSz)
                float PDx     = pvPx * math.exp(falling ? -mSize : mSize)
                float span    = math.abs(PDx - pvPx)
                gIO   := pvIdx
                gPO   := pvPx
                gN    := NN
                gPD   := PDx
                gWup  := span * vlMedian(rus)
                gWdn  := span * vlMedian(rds)
                gSkip := math.round(skipFrac * NN)
                gConf := t
                gId   := projCount
                projCount += 1
                gOn   := true

    // 4–7. Exit of the open trade (against its own projection), then a possible entry.
    var int   posSide      = 0
    var int   posEntryIdx  = na
    var float posEntryPx   = na
    var int   posEntryTime = na
    var int   posProj      = -1
    var int   pIO          = na
    var float pPO          = na
    var int   pN           = na
    var float pPD          = na
    var float pWup         = na
    var float pWdn         = na
    var int   pSkip        = na
    var int   lastEnteredId = -1
    var int   nT      = 0
    var int   nWin    = 0
    var float sRet    = 0.0
    var float sWin    = 0.0
    var float sLoss   = 0.0
    var float sBars   = 0.0
    var float sDays   = 0.0
    var float sSq     = 0.0
    var float medBars = na
    var float medDays = na
    var array<float> tBars = array.new<float>()
    var array<float> tDays = array.new<float>()
    bool  buy      = false
    bool  sell     = false
    int   exitCode = 0       // 1 target, 2 stop, 3 time
    int   exitSide = 0
    float exitRet  = na
    float entryE   = na
    float eLive    = na
    if ok
        if posSide != 0 and t > posEntryIdx
            int iX     = t - pIO
            int reason = 0
            if iX > pN - pSkip
                reason := 3
            else
                float eX = vlPositionE(pPO, pPD, pN, pWup, pWdn, iX, o4)
                if (posSide > 0 ? eX <= -stopE : eX >= stopE)
                    reason := 2
                else if (posSide > 0 ? eX >= 0 : eX <= 0)
                    reason := 1
            if reason != 0
                float ret  = posSide * (close - posEntryPx) / posEntryPx - cost
                float days = (time - posEntryTime) / 86400000.0
                int   nb   = t - posEntryIdx
                nT    += 1
                if ret > 0
                    nWin += 1
                sRet  += ret
                sWin  += math.max(0.0, ret)
                sLoss += math.max(0.0, -ret)
                sBars += nb
                sDays += days
                sSq   += ret * ret
                array.push(tBars, float(nb))
                array.push(tDays, days)
                medBars  := vlMedian(tBars)
                medDays  := vlMedian(tDays)
                exitCode := reason
                exitSide := posSide
                exitRet  := ret
                posSide  := 0
        if gOn and t >= gConf
            int iE = t - gIO
            if iE >= gSkip and iE <= gN - gSkip
                float eE = vlPositionE(gPO, gPD, gN, gWup, gWdn, iE, o4)
                eLive := eE
                float aE = math.abs(eE)
                if posSide == 0 and lastEnteredId != gId and aE >= level and aE < stopE
                    int side = eE < 0 ? 1 : -1
                    posSide      := side
                    posEntryIdx  := t
                    posEntryPx   := close
                    posEntryTime := time
                    posProj      := gId
                    pIO   := gIO
                    pPO   := gPO
                    pN    := gN
                    pPD   := gPD
                    pWup  := gWup
                    pWdn  := gWdn
                    pSkip := gSkip
                    lastEnteredId := gId
                    entryE := eE
                    buy    := side > 0
                    sell   := side < 0

    [buy, sell, exitCode, exitSide, exitRet, entryE, posSide, posEntryPx, posProj, pvKind, pvIdx, pvPx, gOn, gId, gIO, gPO, gN, gPD, gWup, gWdn, gSkip, eLive, pIO, pPO, pN, pPD, pWup, pWdn, nT, nWin, sRet, sWin, sLoss, sBars, sDays, sSq, medBars, medDays, nBars, firstTime]

// The statistics of one timeframe as of its last CLOSED bar. Runs inside request.security:
// on a bar that has not closed yet (the realtime bar, or an unfinished last bar) it returns
// the previous bar's values, so the table never counts a trade on an unconfirmed bar.
vlConfirmedStats(int atrLen, float atrMult, int K, float level, float stopE, float skipFrac, int minN, float cost) =>
    [x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, x7, x8, x9, x10, x11, x12, x13, x14, x15, x16, x17, x18, x19, x20, x21, x22, x23, x24, x25, x26, x27, x28, nT, nWin, sRet, sWin, sLoss, sBars, sDays, sSq, medBars, medDays, nBars, firstTime] = vortexCore(atrLen, atrMult, K, level, stopE, skipFrac, minN, cost)
    bool done = na(time_close) or timenow >= time_close
    [done ? nT : nT[1], done ? nWin : nWin[1], done ? sRet : sRet[1], done ? sWin : sWin[1], done ? sLoss : sLoss[1], done ? sBars : sBars[1], done ? sDays : sDays[1], done ? sSq : sSq[1], done ? medBars : medBars[1], done ? medDays : medDays[1], done ? nBars : nBars[1], firstTime]

// ── run it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[cBuy, cSell, cExit, cExitSide, cExitRet, cEntryE, cPosSide, cPosPx, cPosProj, cPivKind, cPivIdx, cPivPx, cGOn, cGId, cGIO, cGPO, cGN, cGPD, cGWup, cGWdn, cGSkip, cELive, cPIO, cPPO, cPN, cPPD, cPWup, cPWdn, cNT, cNW, cSR, cSW, cSL, cSB, cSD, cSQ, cMB, cMD, cBars, cT0] = vortexCore(atrLenIn, atrMultIn, kIn, levelIn, stopIn, vlSkipFrac, VL_MIN_N, vlCostFrac)

[h4N, h4W, h4R, h4GW, h4GL, h4B, h4D, h4Q, h4MB, h4MD, h4Bars, h4T0] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "240", vlConfirmedStats(atrLenIn, atrMultIn, kIn, levelIn, stopIn, vlSkipFrac, VL_MIN_N, vlCostFrac), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[d1N, d1W, d1R, d1GW, d1GL, d1B, d1D, d1Q, d1MB, d1MD, d1Bars, d1T0] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", vlConfirmedStats(atrLenIn, atrMultIn, kIn, levelIn, stopIn, vlSkipFrac, VL_MIN_N, vlCostFrac), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[w1N, w1W, w1R, w1GW, w1GL, w1B, w1D, w1Q, w1MB, w1MD, w1Bars, w1T0] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", vlConfirmedStats(atrLenIn, atrMultIn, kIn, levelIn, stopIn, vlSkipFrac, VL_MIN_N, vlCostFrac), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
[m1N, m1W, m1R, m1GW, m1GL, m1B, m1D, m1Q, m1MB, m1MD, m1Bars, m1T0] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "M", vlConfirmedStats(atrLenIn, atrMultIn, kIn, levelIn, stopIn, vlSkipFrac, VL_MIN_N, vlCostFrac), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

// Has this bar closed? barstate.isconfirmed alone is true on EVERY historical bar, including a
// last bar that is still forming because the chart was loaded while the market is shut (a
// weekly bar mid-week, a monthly bar mid-month, a 4H bar across a session break). So on the
// last historical bar it also needs time_close to have passed — the same rule the other
// timeframes' rows use in vlConfirmedStats. Realtime bars close on their last update.
bool  vlClosed  = barstate.isconfirmed and (barstate.isrealtime or not barstate.islast or na(time_close) or timenow >= time_close)

// The chart's own state as of its last CLOSED bar (on a bar that has not closed yet, the
// previous bar's): what the projection drawing, the status row and the chart's table row show.
bool  vlNow     = vlClosed
bool  dGOn      = vlNow ? cGOn : cGOn[1]
int   dGId      = vlNow ? cGId : cGId[1]
int   dGIO      = vlNow ? cGIO : cGIO[1]
float dGPO      = vlNow ? cGPO : cGPO[1]
int   dGN       = vlNow ? cGN : cGN[1]
float dGPD      = vlNow ? cGPD : cGPD[1]
float dGWup     = vlNow ? cGWup : cGWup[1]
float dGWdn     = vlNow ? cGWdn : cGWdn[1]
int   dGSkip    = vlNow ? cGSkip : cGSkip[1]
float dELive    = vlNow ? cELive : cELive[1]
int   dPosSide  = vlNow ? cPosSide : nz(cPosSide[1])
float dPosPx    = vlNow ? cPosPx : cPosPx[1]
int   dPosProj  = vlNow ? cPosProj : cPosProj[1]
int   dPIO      = vlNow ? cPIO : cPIO[1]
float dPPO      = vlNow ? cPPO : cPPO[1]
int   dPN       = vlNow ? cPN : cPN[1]
float dPPD      = vlNow ? cPPD : cPPD[1]
float dPWup     = vlNow ? cPWup : cPWup[1]
float dPWdn     = vlNow ? cPWdn : cPWdn[1]
int   lN        = vlNow ? cNT : nz(cNT[1])
int   lW        = vlNow ? cNW : nz(cNW[1])
float lSR       = vlNow ? cSR : nz(cSR[1])
float lSW       = vlNow ? cSW : nz(cSW[1])
float lSL       = vlNow ? cSL : nz(cSL[1])
float lSB       = vlNow ? cSB : nz(cSB[1])
float lSD       = vlNow ? cSD : nz(cSD[1])
float lSQ       = vlNow ? cSQ : nz(cSQ[1])
float lMB       = vlNow ? cMB : cMB[1]
float lMD       = vlNow ? cMD : cMD[1]
int   lBars     = vlNow ? cBars : nz(cBars[1])

// ── signals on the chart (closed bars only; never moved or deleted) ──────────
vlPct(float x) =>
    na(x) ? "—" : (x >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(x * 100.0, "0.00") + "%"

var int vlLastEntryBar = na
if vlClosed
    if cExit != 0
        string exGlyph = cExit == 1 ? "✓" : cExit == 2 ? "✕" : "⏱"
        string exWhy   = cExit == 1 ? "هدف — عاد السعر إلى المتجه (target: back to the vector)" : cExit == 2 ? "وقف — |e| ≥ " + str.tostring(stopIn) + " (stop)" : "وقت — انتهت مدة الإسقاط (time: past N − skip)"
        color  exCol   = cExit == 1 ? VL_BUY : cExit == 2 ? VL_SELL : VL_MUTED
        string exHold  = na(vlLastEntryBar) ? "" : "\nالمدة " + str.tostring(bar_index - vlLastEntryBar) + " شمعة"
        label.new(bar_index, close, exGlyph, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(exCol, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, tooltip = "خروج " + (cExitSide > 0 ? "من شراء" : "من بيع") + " — " + exWhy + "\nالعائد بعد التكلفة " + vlPct(cExitRet) + exHold)
    if cBuy or cSell
        vlLastEntryBar := bar_index
        string enTip = "e = " + str.tostring(cEntryE, "0.00") + " · الدخول عند الإغلاق " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + "\nالهدف: المتجه · الوقف: |e| ≥ " + str.tostring(stopIn)
        if cBuy
            label.new(bar_index, low, "شراء", xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.belowbar, style = label.style_label_up, color = VL_BUY, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, tooltip = "شراء عند الجدار السفلي — " + enTip)
        else
            label.new(bar_index, high, "بيع", xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.abovebar, style = label.style_label_down, color = VL_SELL, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, tooltip = "بيع عند الجدار العلوي — " + enTip)
    if showPivIn and cPivKind != 0
        label.new(cPivIdx, cPivPx, "", xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = cPivKind == 1 ? yloc.abovebar : yloc.belowbar, style = cPivKind == 1 ? label.style_triangledown : label.style_triangleup, color = color.new(VL_VEC, 40), size = size.tiny, tooltip = (cPivKind == 1 ? "قمة" : "قاع") + " مؤكدة عند " + str.tostring(cPivPx, format.mintick) + " — تأكدت بعد " + str.tostring(bar_index - cPivIdx) + " شمعة")

// Closed bars only, like the table's e: na while a bar is still forming (and where |e| is ±∞).
plot(vlClosed and math.abs(cELive) < VL_E_BIG ? cELive : na, "e (الموضع بين الجدارين)", color = VL_VEC, display = display.data_window)

// Create alerts with the frequency "Once Per Bar Close" (عند إغلاق الشمعة).
alertcondition(cBuy and vlClosed, "O→D Vortex — شراء", "O→D Vortex Live: شراء (buy) {{ticker}} {{interval}} عند {{close}}")
alertcondition(cSell and vlClosed, "O→D Vortex — بيع", "O→D Vortex Live: بيع (sell) {{ticker}} {{interval}} عند {{close}}")
alertcondition(cExit != 0 and vlClosed, "O→D Vortex — خروج", "O→D Vortex Live: خروج (exit) {{ticker}} {{interval}} عند {{close}}")

// ── the live projection (redrawn on the last bar only) ───────────────────────
// Points beyond 500 bars into the future are cut off (TradingView's drawing limit).
vlDrawGeometry(array<polyline> polys, array<label> labs, int iO, float PO, int N, float PD, float wUp, float wDn, float lvl, bool band, int transp, string tag) =>
    int iMax = math.min(N, bar_index + VL_FUTURE - iO)
    if iMax >= 1
        array<chart.point> pVec = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> pUp  = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> pDn  = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> bUp  = array.new<chart.point>()
        array<chart.point> bDn  = array.new<chart.point>()
        for i = 0 to iMax
            float vec = PO + ((PD - PO) * i) / N
            float u   = 2.0 * i / N - 1.0
            float shp = math.sqrt(math.max(0.0, 1.0 - u * u))
            array.push(pVec, chart.point.from_index(iO + i, vec))
            array.push(pUp, chart.point.from_index(iO + i, vec + wUp * shp))
            array.push(pDn, chart.point.from_index(iO + i, vec - wDn * shp))
            if band
                array.push(bUp, chart.point.from_index(iO + i, vec + lvl * wUp * shp))
                array.push(bDn, chart.point.from_index(iO + i, vec - lvl * wDn * shp))
        array.push(polys, polyline.new(pVec, curved = false, closed = false, xloc = xloc.bar_index, line_color = color.new(VL_VEC, transp), line_style = line.style_dashed, line_width = 1))
        array.push(polys, polyline.new(pUp, curved = false, closed = false, xloc = xloc.bar_index, line_color = color.new(VL_SELL, transp), line_style = line.style_solid, line_width = 2))
        array.push(polys, polyline.new(pDn, curved = false, closed = false, xloc = xloc.bar_index, line_color = color.new(VL_BUY, transp), line_style = line.style_solid, line_width = 2))
        if band
            array.push(polys, polyline.new(bUp, curved = false, closed = false, xloc = xloc.bar_index, line_color = color.new(VL_SELL, math.min(90, transp + 40)), line_style = line.style_dotted, line_width = 1))
            array.push(polys, polyline.new(bDn, curved = false, closed = false, xloc = xloc.bar_index, line_color = color.new(VL_BUY, math.min(90, transp + 40)), line_style = line.style_dotted, line_width = 1))
        array.push(labs, label.new(iO, PO, "O" + tag, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_label_center, color = color.new(VL_VEC, math.min(90, transp + 60)), textcolor = color.new(color.white, transp), size = size.tiny, tooltip = "O — المحور الذي بدأ منه الإسقاط"))
        if iO + N <= bar_index + VL_FUTURE
            array.push(labs, label.new(iO + N, PD, "D" + tag, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_label_center, color = color.new(VL_VEC, math.min(90, transp + 60)), textcolor = color.new(color.white, transp), size = size.tiny, tooltip = "D المتوقَّع: O × exp(∓ وسيط حجم آخر K موجات) بعد N = " + str.tostring(N) + " شمعة"))
    true

var array<polyline> vlPolys = array.new<polyline>()
var array<label>    vlGeomLabels = array.new<label>()
if barstate.islast
    while array.size(vlPolys) > 0
        polyline.delete(array.pop(vlPolys))
    while array.size(vlGeomLabels) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(vlGeomLabels))
    if showProjIn
        if dGOn
            vlDrawGeometry(vlPolys, vlGeomLabels, dGIO, dGPO, dGN, dGPD, dGWup, dGWdn, levelIn, showBandIn, 0, "")
        // The open trade's own projection, faded, when the live one has replaced it.
        if dPosSide != 0 and (not dGOn or dPosProj != dGId)
            vlDrawGeometry(vlPolys, vlGeomLabels, dPIO, dPPO, dPN, dPPD, dPWup, dPWdn, levelIn, false, 60, "′")

// ── per-timeframe table (filled on the last bar only) ────────────────────────
vlTablePosition(string s) =>
    switch s
        "أعلى اليسار" => position.top_left
        "أسفل اليمين" => position.bottom_right
        "أسفل اليسار" => position.bottom_left
        => position.top_right

// Columns are laid out right to left, so the timeframe name sits on the right.
vlCell(table tb, int k, int row, string txt, color fg, color bg, string tip) =>
    table.cell(tb, VL_NCOL - 1 - k, row, txt, text_color = fg, bgcolor = bg, text_size = size.small, tooltip = tip)
    true

// st = [n, wins, Σret, Σwin, Σloss, Σbars, Σdays, Σret², median bars, median days, bars, first time]
vlStatsRow(table tb, int row, string name, bool hl, array<float> st) =>
    color bg = hl ? VL_THL : VL_TBG
    color fg = hl ? color.white : color.new(color.white, 15)
    int   n  = int(nz(array.get(st, 0)))
    int   w  = int(nz(array.get(st, 1)))
    float sR = nz(array.get(st, 2))
    float sW = nz(array.get(st, 3))
    float sL = nz(array.get(st, 4))
    float sB = nz(array.get(st, 5))
    float sD = nz(array.get(st, 6))
    float sQ = nz(array.get(st, 7))
    float mB = array.get(st, 8)
    float mD = array.get(st, 9)
    float nb = array.get(st, 10)
    float t0 = array.get(st, 11)
    float ex = n > 0 ? sR / n : na
    float hw = n > 1 ? 1.96 * math.sqrt(math.max(0.0, (sQ - n * ex * ex) / (n - 1))) / math.sqrt(n) : na
    color exCol = na(hw) ? fg : ex - hw > 0 ? VL_BUY : ex + hw < 0 ? VL_SELL : VL_MUTED
    string pf = sL > 0 ? str.tostring(sW / sL, "0.00") : sW > 0 ? "∞" : "—"
    vlCell(tb, 0, row, name, fg, bg, "")
    vlCell(tb, 1, row, str.tostring(n), n < 30 ? VL_WARN : fg, bg, n < 30 ? "عينة صغيرة (أقل من 30 صفقة): أي نسبة هنا هامشها واسع جداً — small sample" : "")
    vlCell(tb, 2, row, n > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * w / n, "0.0") + "%  (" + str.tostring(w) + "/" + str.tostring(n) + ")" : "—", fg, bg, "")
    vlCell(tb, 3, row, n > 0 ? str.tostring(mB, "0.0") + " شمعة · " + str.tostring(mD, "0.0") + " يوم" : "—", fg, bg, "")
    vlCell(tb, 4, row, n > 0 ? str.tostring(sB / n, "0.0") + " شمعة · " + str.tostring(sD / n, "0.0") + " يوم" : "—", fg, bg, "")
    vlCell(tb, 5, row, n > 0 ? vlPct(ex) + (na(hw) ? "" : "  ±" + str.tostring(hw * 100.0, "0.00") + "%") : "—", exCol, bg, "")
    vlCell(tb, 6, row, n > 0 ? pf : "—", fg, bg, "")
    vlCell(tb, 7, row, (na(nb) or na(t0)) ? "—" : str.tostring(int(nb)) + " شمعة منذ " + str.format_time(int(t0), "yyyy-MM-dd", syminfo.timezone), color.new(fg, 30), bg, "")
    true

vlTfName() =>
    string s = timeframe.period
    if timeframe.isminutes and timeframe.multiplier % 60 == 0
        s := str.tostring(int(timeframe.multiplier / 60)) + "H"
    s

int  vlChartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
bool is4h = vlChartSec == timeframe.in_seconds("240")
bool isD  = vlChartSec == timeframe.in_seconds("D")
bool isW  = vlChartSec == timeframe.in_seconds("W")
bool isM  = vlChartSec == timeframe.in_seconds("M")

var table vlTable = table.new(vlTablePosition(tablePosIn), VL_NCOL, VL_NROW, bgcolor = VL_TBG, frame_color = color.new(VL_MUTED, 50), frame_width = 1, border_color = color.new(VL_MUTED, 75), border_width = 1)

if barstate.islast and showTableIn
    // header
    vlCell(vlTable, 0, 0, "الفريم", color.white, VL_THEAD, "Timeframe. The highlighted row is this chart's own timeframe and matches the labels on the chart.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 1, 0, "الصفقات", color.white, VL_THEAD, "Closed trades. A trade still open is not counted.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 2, 0, "نسبة الربح", color.white, VL_THEAD, "Share of closed trades with a return above 0 after cost. On its own it does not say whether the method makes money: a high win rate with small wins and large losses still loses. Read it with the mean return and the profit factor.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 3, 0, "المدة المعتادة (الوسيط)", color.white, VL_THEAD, "Typical (median) holding time: half the trades are shorter, half longer — in bars and in calendar days.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 4, 0, "متوسط المدة", color.white, VL_THEAD, "Mean holding time, in bars and in calendar days.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 5, 0, "متوسط العائد/صفقة", color.white, VL_THEAD, "Expectancy: mean return per trade after cost, ± a rough 95 % interval (normal approximation). Green only if the whole interval is above 0, red only if it is all below 0; grey means it cannot be told apart from 0.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 6, 0, "عامل الربح", color.white, VL_THEAD, "Profit factor: gross wins ÷ gross losses. Below 1 loses money.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 7, 0, "البيانات", color.white, VL_THEAD, "How many bars of this timeframe the row was computed on, and the first one. Results depend on where the loaded history starts; other timeframes only get roughly the chart's date range — open the indicator on that timeframe's chart for its full history.")

    // The chart's own timeframe uses the chart's own run, so its row matches the labels.
    array<float> rowLocal = array.from(float(lN), float(lW), lSR, lSW, lSL, lSB, lSD, lSQ, lMB, lMD, float(lBars), float(cT0))
    array<float> row4h    = is4h ? rowLocal : array.from(float(nz(h4N)), float(nz(h4W)), h4R, h4GW, h4GL, h4B, h4D, h4Q, h4MB, h4MD, float(h4Bars), float(h4T0))
    array<float> rowD     = isD ? rowLocal : array.from(float(nz(d1N)), float(nz(d1W)), d1R, d1GW, d1GL, d1B, d1D, d1Q, d1MB, d1MD, float(d1Bars), float(d1T0))
    array<float> rowW     = isW ? rowLocal : array.from(float(nz(w1N)), float(nz(w1W)), w1R, w1GW, w1GL, w1B, w1D, w1Q, w1MB, w1MD, float(w1Bars), float(w1T0))
    array<float> rowM     = isM ? rowLocal : array.from(float(nz(m1N)), float(nz(m1W)), m1R, m1GW, m1GL, m1B, m1D, m1Q, m1MB, m1MD, float(m1Bars), float(m1T0))
    vlStatsRow(vlTable, 1, "4H", is4h, row4h)
    vlStatsRow(vlTable, 2, "يومي", isD, rowD)
    vlStatsRow(vlTable, 3, "أسبوعي", isW, rowW)
    vlStatsRow(vlTable, 4, "شهري", isM, rowM)
    if not (is4h or isD or isW or isM)
        vlStatsRow(vlTable, 5, "الحالي · " + vlTfName(), true, rowLocal)

    // status of this chart, as of its last closed bar
    string posTxt  = dPosSide > 0 ? "مركز: شراء مفتوح من " + str.tostring(dPosPx, format.mintick) : dPosSide < 0 ? "مركز: بيع مفتوح من " + str.tostring(dPosPx, format.mintick) : "مركز: لا يوجد"
    string projTxt = dGOn ? "إسقاط حي: N = " + str.tostring(dGN) + " · D ≈ " + str.tostring(dGPD, format.mintick) : "لا إسقاط حي — بانتظار القمة/القاع التالي"
    vlCell(vlTable, 0, 6, "الآن · " + vlTfName(), color.white, VL_THEAD, "This chart's state as of its last closed bar.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 1, 6, "e = " + (na(dELive) ? "—" : math.abs(dELive) >= VL_E_BIG ? (dELive > 0 ? "+∞" : "−∞") : str.tostring(dELive, "0.00")), color.white, VL_THEAD, "Position between the walls: +1 upper wall, 0 vector, −1 lower wall. A trade needs contact ≤ |e| < stop.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 2, 6, posTxt, color.white, VL_THEAD, "")
    vlCell(vlTable, 3, 6, projTxt, color.white, VL_THEAD, "")
    vlCell(vlTable, 4, 6, "", color.white, VL_THEAD, "")
    vlCell(vlTable, 5, 6, "الحكم بمتوسط العائد وهامشه، لا بنسبة الربح", VL_WARN, VL_THEAD, "Judge a timeframe by the mean return and its interval, not by the win rate.")
    vlCell(vlTable, 6, 6, "", color.white, VL_THEAD, "")
    vlCell(vlTable, 7, 6, "", color.white, VL_THEAD, "")
